From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: bind flowtable entries by orig tuple + trace check_skb

The flowtable now delivers flows to the driver (conntrack [HW_OFFLOAD])
but every PPE entry stays UNB. airoha_ppe_foe_compare_entry byte-compares
the full entry (including L2 MACs/ethertype and the NAT new tuple), but
hardware entries created by the NPU on RX carry incomplete L2 fields and
a different new tuple, so the compare always rejects them and the
flowtable entry is never bound.

Compare only the flow identity (the original tuple) for IPv4/IPv6, and
also require the hardware entry packet type to match. Add a ratelimited
trace in airoha_ppe_check_skb to confirm the HIT_UNBIND trigger fires.
Remove the trace once binding is confirmed.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
--- fork_clean_lf.c	2026-08-19 23:41:31
+++ fork_clean_lf.mod.c	2026-08-19 23:41:40
@@ -738,17 +738,34 @@
 					 struct airoha_foe_entry *hwe)
 {
 	int type = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PACKET_TYPE, e->data.ib1);
-	int len;
 
 	if ((hwe->ib1 ^ e->data.ib1) & AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_UDP)
 		return false;
 
-	if (type > PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_DSLITE)
-		len = offsetof(struct airoha_foe_entry, ipv6.data);
-	else
-		len = offsetof(struct airoha_foe_entry, ipv4.ib2);
+	if (FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PACKET_TYPE, hwe->ib1) != type)
+		return false;
 
-	return !memcmp(&e->data.d, &hwe->d, len - sizeof(hwe->ib1));
+	/* Compare only the flow identity (the original tuple). Hardware
+	 * entries created by the NPU on RX carry incomplete L2 fields (zero
+	 * MACs / ethertype), so a byte-for-byte compare of the whole entry
+	 * would always reject them and the flowtable entries would never be
+	 * bound to the PPE.
+	 */
+	switch (type) {
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_HNAPT:
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_ROUTE:
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_DSLITE:
+		return !memcmp(&e->data.ipv4.orig_tuple,
+			       &hwe->ipv4.orig_tuple,
+			       sizeof(struct airoha_foe_ipv4_tuple));
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_3T:
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_5T:
+	case PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_6RD:
+		return !memcmp(&e->data.ipv6.src_ip, &hwe->ipv6.src_ip,
+			       offsetof(struct airoha_foe_ipv6, data));
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
 }
 
 static int airoha_ppe_foe_commit_sram_entry(struct airoha_ppe *ppe, u32 hash)
@@ -1725,6 +1742,9 @@
 	if (hash > ppe_hash_mask)
 		return;
 
+	pr_warn_ratelimited("airoha_ppe: check_skb hash=%04x rx_wlan=%d\n",
+			    hash, rx_wlan);
+
 	/* Flows addressed to the router itself must be delivered to the CPU
 	 * and must never be offloaded to the PPE. Committing a local flow
 	 * produces a broken PPE entry that drops traffic after the first
